  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday through next Tuesday)\nIssued at 125 PM CDT Tue Jul 28 2026\n\nSeasonably hot temperatures and triple-digit heat indices will be\nthe main weather story across South Central Texas heading into \nthe weekend as the region remains under the influence of mid level\nridging centered over the Desert Southwest. Temperatures will \ngradually rise each afternoon, with widespread highs approaching \nthe triple-digits (100-103 degrees) by Thursday and Friday. \nSlightly lower humidity should keep heat indices just below heat \nadvisory through the end of the week. However, humidity is \nexpected to increase this weekend in combination with the triple-\ndigit heat, which may result in the issuance of heat headlines \nacross portions of the region. \n\nMid level ridging is expected to shift west late this weekend and\ninto early next week, which may open the door for the return of\nlow precipitation chances as upper level trough translates across\nthe Plains and sends a cold front southward. However, there\nremains uncertainty among guidance on this setup so continue to\ncheck back for updates.",
